In the pre-registered replications, we used the same survey as in the original study, and therefore the same instructions, procedures, images, and questions. These studies did not deviate from the original study in any discernible way, except that our consent form was necessarily different, our exclusion rules were slightly different [
4
], and we added an attention check to the last page of the survey to help us measure participant quality. After exclusions, we wound up with 1,099 participants in Replication 1 (~7.5 times the original sample size) and 1,555 participants in Replication 2 (~10.7 times the original sample size)
